    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0169" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">637.116/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-22T11:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 22,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:25
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>219. President Menocal yesterday noon showed some displeasure because Vice
                    President Nuñez, who left for Washington last Monday morning, had announced he
                    would there discuss the rice situation.</p>
                <p>While President Menocal’s intentions seem to be all right he allowed his
                    Secretary of the Treasury to prepare in an anti-American spirit the decree of
                    September 8th [<hi rendition="#italic">6th</hi>] which not only does not live up
                    to the agreement of August 17th but renders more difficult than before its
                    issuance (if that be possible) practical solution of rice problem. New plan of
                    settlement by price fixing now being discussed gives some suggestion of
                    hope.</p>
                <p>I may be able to induce Menocal to make another effort. Chances would be improved
                    if I had stiff telegram from Department to show to Menocal confidentially. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
